      "writtenOn": "2014-12-10T04:24:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "thanks your suggestion, but I have a question about if caller is system server, throwing uncaught exception will let system server died, how do you think if any other way to prevent such case? shall we need to judge if caller is system server than catch exception \u0026 re-throw exception for other process?",
      "parentUuid": "040206f8_21bc2a5d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "5ca264d73eab003c335f363613d890dd90cc4894",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a4077a51_9084949e",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1057059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-12-10T06:54:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since null is not a valid input to this method, we should add checks at the call point in the system server to make sure null will not be passed to this RPC. Fro example, AMS.dumpHeap() already checks to make sure fd is not null. We can also add a check there for file path isn\u0027t null and throw an illegal argument exception if it is.",
      "parentUuid": "24fb8a87_0cfd377c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "5ca264d73eab003c335f363613d890dd90cc4894",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e426d2f7_ed9b814d",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1023708
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-12-10T14:18:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks your feedback, but I found in AMS.dumpHeap(), will pass to ActivityThread.dumpHeap() to dump heap by message, if any exception thrown, it could not be caught in AMS side.\nBeside, even doing fd check is fine in AMS side, it may also have chance to fail in native side due to fd leak or dup fd fail for some reasons. (i.e. storage full.), RuntimeException still can not be prevented to throw back.\nso I change another way to catch RuntimeException, then check if caller is non-system process, still throw back to process, only catch exception for caller is system process to prevent system crash.",
      "parentUuid": "a4077a51_9084949e",
      "revId": "5ca264d73eab003c335f363613d890dd90cc4894",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
